</div>
  <p>The list also always contains an integer in the last element, which is a status code indicating the outcome of the path query:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>If llGetStaticPath() finds a path, it will return waypoint vectors and will return a status code of 0, for success</li>
    <li>If llGetStaticPath() cannot find a path for some reason, it only returns the status code, indicating the sort of error. The error codes correspond to the constants in <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Path_update" target="_blank">path_update</a> (e.g. PU_FAILURE_INVALID_START is returned if the start vector is not near the nav mesh)</li>
  </ul>
